            <div xml:id="d230">

                <pb facs="0410" n="314" sameAs="frus:frus1931-41v01/pg314"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/8682: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-07-08T17:00:00+09:00">July 8, 1937—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received July 8—6:29 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>185. We are informed by the Foreign Office that official Japanese reports from
                    Peiping indicate that prospects are favorable for settlement of the brush which
                    took place this morning near Peiping between Japanese and Chinese troops. It was
                    stated at the Foreign Office that <pb facs="0411" n="315" xml:id="pg315"/> “our
                    military people seem to believe that the firing by Chinese troops which started
                    the incident was not premeditated.”</p>
                <p>Repeated to Peiping.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
